  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "@lijian-ui/dsh-term",
      "text": "Panel-style local terminal for the DSH web GUI.\n\n- **Real PTY sessions** via [`node-pty`](https://github.com/microsoft/node-pty) — a genuine local shell, not a curated command runner.\n- **Multi-tab terminal panel** built on [xterm.js](https://xtermjs.org/), docked in the right-side panel (alongside `@lijian-ui/dsh-file-manager`).\n- **Workspace cwd** — each session starts in the current workspace root.\n- **Hot-pluggable** — loaded as a profile bundle; no changes to DSH source are required."
    },
    {
      "section": "@lijian-ui/dsh-term",
      "text": "> This is the **A edition**: local user terminal only. A planned **B edition** adds SSH connections and per-session shell selection."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```bash\ndsh plugin add @lijian-ui/dsh-term\n```\n\nOr add `@lijian-ui/dsh-term` to your profile's `bundles` / `dependencies` and reference it from `cordis.yml`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Behavior",
      "text": "- Default state is **collapsed** (closed). Open it from the right-side panel launcher (the \"终端\" button) — it docks as the rightmost column next to the file-manager panel.\n- Sessions are managed by a host-side service (`src/host/pty-service.ts`) exposed over loopback-only HTTP + SSE routes (`src/host/routes.ts`). The client renders them with xterm.js and syncs resize/input."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```bash\nnpm install\nnpm run build      # tsc -b && tsdown -> lib/\nnpm run watch      # rebuild on change\nnpm test           # vitest"
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "Apache-2.0"
    }
  ],
